<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pieter Bruegel the Elder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1525–1569</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pieter Bruegel the Elder was the leading Netherlandish painter of the sixteenth century, active in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> and from 1563 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, where he died in 1569. He is famous for landscapes and scenes of peasant life such as The Hunters in the Snow and The Peasant Wedding, as well as The Tower of Babel and his painting of Netherlandish proverbs. His sons Pieter Brueghel the Younger and Jan Brueghel the Elder continued the family tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pieter-bruegel-the-elder.jpg" alt="Pieter Bruegel the Elder" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pieter Brueghel the Elder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pieter_Bruegel_the_Elder_-_The_Painter_and_the_Buyer,_ca._1566_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
